course: dictionary
lesson: 1838
title: The coccyx, or tailbone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from science, and their meaning is often given right in the sentence. «The tailbone, or coccyx, is a few tiny vertebrae fused together.» The two names mean the same thing, so the sentence tells you that coccyx is another word for tailbone.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «A fall on it hurts» tells you the coccyx is a part of your body that can get hurt, and that it is near your bottom. Vertebrae are the bones of your spine, so the coccyx is at the very bottom of the spine.
explain: Some sentences tell you where a body part came from. «The tailbone is a leftover of the tails of our ancestors» means that people who lived long ago, our ancestors, had tails, and the coccyx is what is left of one. Parts like this are called vestigial, and they may now have new jobs.
fact: Coccyx means the tailbone, the small bone at the very bottom of your spine.
fact: The coccyx is made of tiny bones joined together.
fact: The coccyx is also called the tailbone.
fact: Muscles still attach to the coccyx, so a fall on your bottom can hurt it.
fact: Science lessons say the coccyx is a leftover of a tail from long-ago ancestors.
exercise: «The tailbone, or coccyx, is a few tiny vertebrae fused together.» What is another name for the coccyx? | Muscle | *Tailbone | Spine | Ancestor
exercise: Where in your body is the coccyx? | Top of your head | *At the very bottom of your spine | Inside your ear | In your elbow
exercise: Why does a fall on the coccyx hurt? | Because it is very long | *Because muscles still attach to it | Because it is made of soft jelly | Because it is made of glass
test: Mia falls on her bottom and says her coccyx hurts. Where does it hurt? | Her neck | *Her tailbone, at the bottom of her spine | Her wrist | Her knee
test: «Such leftover parts are called vestigial, and they may have new jobs.» What might a leftover part from long-ago ancestors have now? | A new shape of tail | A place in the ear | Nothing at all, and it must always be removed | *A new job
exam: «The coccyx is what is left of a tail, and it still anchors muscles.» What does anchors mean here? | Breaks something into pieces | Lets something go | Makes something louder | *Holds something in place
